1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
He attacked a navy of a thousand

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,760
ships with twenty boats full of straw

3
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:04,000
men.

4
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:06,020
You see, his own commander wants him

5
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:08,020
gone, so he orders a hundred thousand

6
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:09,060
arrows in ten days.

7
00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:11,080
He says, "I only need three."

8
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:12,760
"Fail, and you lose your head."

9
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:14,080
Then for two whole days,

10
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:14,780
he does nothing.

11
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:16,340
No blacksmiths, no feathers,

12
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:17,520
not a single arrow.

13
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:18,440
On the third night,

14
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:20,340
he wraps twenty boats in straw and

15
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:21,660
fills them with straw soldiers.

16
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:23,720
His friend asks, "Are we going to

17
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:25,320
war, or scaring crows?"

18
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:27,540
Before dawn, a thick fog swallows the

19
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:29,040
river, and he sails straight at the

20
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:30,720
enemy camp, pounding war drums.

21
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:32,860
The enemy general hears an attack he

22
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:34,540
can't see, and he won't risk his

23
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:35,160
ships in that fog.

24
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:36,600
So he does the safe thing:

25
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:37,320
"Archers!

26
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:38,100
Shoot at the drums!"

27
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:40,460
Thousands of arrows slam into the straw,

28
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:42,020
until the boats start to tip.

29
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:43,360
So he turns them around to fill

30
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:43,920
up the other side.

31
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:45,900
You see, straw grabs an arrow and

32
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:47,420
won't let go, and in fog,

33
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,520
a straw man looks exactly like a

34
00:00:49,520 --> 00:00:49,880
real one.

35
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:50,960
As the sun burns through,

36
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:52,300
his boats turn for home,

37
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:54,080
so loaded they barely float,

38
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:56,060
and his whole crew shouts back across

39
00:00:56,060 --> 00:00:57,680
the water: "Thanks for the arrows!"

